===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|primerose}}, from {{der|en|fro|primerose}}, from {{der|en|ML.|prima||first}} + {{m|la|rosa||rose}}. The reason it was called this might be that some primroses are among the first flowers to bloom in the spring.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɪm.ɹoʊz/|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɪm.ɹəʊz/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-primrose.wav|a=Southern England}}

